latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Analyze the input grid:\n   a. Determine grid dimensions (should be 11x11).\n   b. Identify the three sections (top: rows 0-2, middle: rows 4-6, bottom: rows 8-10).\n   c. Count the number of red and blue cells in each section.\n\n2. Create a deep copy of the input grid to modify.\n\n3. Process the top section (rows 0-2):\n   a. Convert all non-black cells to blue.\n   b. Identify 2-3 positions for red cells:\n      - Prioritize original red cell positions if they exist.\n      - If fewer than 2 red cells existed, add red cells to reach 2-3.\n      - Distribute red cells across different columns if possible.\n   c. Place red cells in the identified positions.\n\n4. Process the middle section (rows 4-6):\n   a. Determine the original dominant color.\n   b. Calculate the inversion ratio:\n      - If original dominance was >70%, aim for 75-80% new dominant color.\n      - If original dominance was 60-70%, aim for 65-75% new dominant color.\n      - If original dominance was 50-60%, aim for 60-70% new dominant color.\n   c. Iterate through cells:\n      - Invert colors based on the calculated ratio.\n      - Attempt to preserve some original patterns by keeping about 20-30% of cells in their original color, prioritizing cells that form small clusters or lines.\n\n5. Process the bottom section (rows 8-10):\n   a. Convert all non-black cells to red.\n   b. Identify one position for a blue cell:\n      - Prefer an original blue cell position if it exists.\n      - If no blue cell existed, place one in the center or second row of the section.\n   c. Place the blue cell in the identified position.\n\n6. Preserve all black cells (value 0) throughout the grid:\n   - Ensure that cells with value 0 in the input grid remain 0 in the output grid.\n\n7. Final pass:\n   a. Verify that each section meets the required criteria:\n      - Top: Predominantly blue with 2-3 red cells.\n      - Middle: Inverted dominance with a mix of both colors.\n      - Bottom: Predominantly red with exactly one blue cell.\n   b. Make minor adjustments if necessary to meet these criteria.\n\n8. Return the transformed grid.\n\nThis plan should provide a general solution that can handle various input distributions while consistently producing outputs that meet the challenge criteria. It incorporates flexibility in the middle section to account for different levels of color dominance and attempts to preserve some of the original patterns, which should help it adapt to different input scenarios."
